<title>FRANCE: Africa top 1996 air import source for Paris perish.</title>
<headline>Africa top 1996 air import source for Paris perish.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vegetables from Africa were the top perishable imports in 1996 at Charles de Gaulle and Orly airports with 12,247 tonnes handled, a rise of 7.4 percent over the previous year, French ministry of transport figures showed.</p>
<p>Meat imports from North America rose 7.2 percent to 11,414 tonnes and were also up 22.1 percent at 4,558 tonnes from the Central, South America and Caribbean region, the figures showed.</p>
<p>     Region	     Produce	   1996	 Pct change</p>
<p>						imports	over 1995</p>
<p>						(tonnes)</p>
<p>  1.  Africa	    Vegetables	12,247	up  7.4</p>
<p>  2.  N.America	 Meat		11,414	up  7.2</p>
<p>  3.  Africa	    Fruit &amp; Nuts     8,560    down  8.6</p>
<p>  4.  N. America	Fish &amp; Seafood   6,587	up  7.8</p>
<p>  5.  Cen/S.Amer	Meat		 4,558	up 22.1</p>
<p>Caribbean</p>
<p>  6.  Africa	    Fish &amp; Seafood   3,816	up  9.2</p>
<p>  7.  Cen/S.Amer	Fruit &amp; Nuts     3,617	up 17.3</p>
<p>Caribbean</p>
<p>  8.  Mid-East/Asia   Vegetables	 1,949	up  7.2</p>
<p>  9.  Mid-East/Asia   Fruit &amp; Nuts     1,929	up  7.5</p>
<p>  10. Cen/S.Amer	Citrus fruit     1,624    down 14.3</p>
<p>Caribbean</p>
<p>  11. Cen/S.Amer	Vegetables	 1,514	    n/a</p>
<p>Caribbean</p>
